  "_about": "Route dungeons (src/dungeon, src/states/overworld/dungeon.py). An area listed here is walked on a map instead of the route menu. floors: how many floors (stairs between them). style: field, forest or cave. size: [width, height] in tiles. wild: [fewest, most] wild Pokemon on a floor. loot: per_floor [fewest, most] loose items, and items {item: weight} (weights, not percents; POKE_BALLS go to the Poke Ball count). tm_spots: fixed TM spot ids (the TM in each is picked once per save, among the TMs not owned yet). Anything left out comes from DEFAULT. style also building (walls and floor tiles) or sea (you surf the floor). ponds: how many rooms on a floor get a pond (fishing). descend: the floors go down (1F, B1F...). An area in zones (the Pokemon Tower, the Seafoam Islands, the Safari Zone) gets a floor for each zone instead of floors. figure_floors: {figure text: floor} puts a figure on that floor. zones_per_floor: several zones side by side on one floor that many times as wide (the Johto Safari Zone).",
